From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: android-kitkat-tls12 <android-kitkat-tls12@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/31] Port of 336e8eb: enable support for TLSv1.2 cipher
 suites in SSLSocket

Port of external/conscrypt 336e8eb9510cdad7c7a5f73ead3529d558cb0d08
("Enable support for TLSv1.2 cipher suites in SSLSocket", 5.0): the 33
TLS 1.2 rows (AES-GCM, AES-CBC with SHA-256/SHA-384, NULL-SHA256) are
added to STANDARD_TO_OPENSSL_CIPHER_SUITES with the OpenSSL names of our
1.0.1e (ssl/tls1.h TLS1_TXT_*). They become *supported*, not default;
the default list is a later commit of this series.

Test changes taken with it, so that the tree stays green:
- libcore 9e73d3f497461c5bd788bcfb7882e78c016e5876 (same Change-Id),
  StandardNames only: the TLS 1.2 names move from addNeither/addRi to the
  OpenSSL set, and CIPHER_SUITES_SSLENGINE drops *_SHA256/*_SHA384 (the
  Harmony SSLEngine has no TLS 1.2 suites). Its SSLSocket javadoc table is
  not taken: the 4.4 SSLSocket.java has no such table. The KitKat
  CIPHER_SUITES_DEFAULT_SSLENGINE list does not exist, so its second loop
  is dropped; CIPHER_SUITE_FALLBACK (6c9609af5f) stays filtered;
- conscrypt 64a1e90e8337da9bb36370e1b2b4e654d4ddc3fb: CipherSuiteTest
  expects CipherSuite.getByName() == null for *_SHA256/*_SHA384;
- KitKat only: SSLSocketTest.test_SSLSocket_getSupportedCipherSuites_connect
  enables TLSv1.2 on both sockets for the TLS 1.2-only suites, because the
  4.4 client default protocols stop at TLSv1 (until the default-protocols commit) and OpenSSL never
  offers such a suite below TLS 1.2; TestSSLSocketPair.connect() gains an
  overload with the protocols.

Needs the port of 2d089e18: before it, a server socket with any TLS
1.2 suite enabled threw a NullPointerException in CipherSuite.getByName().
